{
  "comment": "JGit org.eclipse.jgit.lib.Config.getEnum() resolves the configured value by reflectively calling <enumDefault>.getClass().getMethod(\"values\").invoke(null) in Config.allValuesOf — UNCONDITIONALLY, even when the config key is unset. In a GraalVM native image values() is stripped unless registered, so the call throws IllegalArgumentException 'Enumerated values of type X not available' (JGitText.enumValuesNotAvailable). First seen 2026-06-21 on GraphQL git.pullRequests[].mergeable (ResolveMerger reads diff.algorithm -> DiffAlgorithm$SupportedAlgorithm). This list is the COMPLETE set of enum defaults across EVERY Config.getEnum call site in jgit 7.6.0 (whole-jar javap trace), so every reachable git operation in this server + git-jobs (server-side merge, upload-pack/receive-pack transport, fsck, dircache, object hashing, submodule/fetch sync) is covered, not just the merge path. All enums are 'final class' (no constant-specific bodies, so registering values() on the type is sufficient) EXCEPT BranchConfig$BranchRebaseMode, which has a constant-specific body ($1): its default constant's getClass() may be the $1 subclass, so $1 is registered with allPublicMethods to expose the inherited static values(). Re-run the whole-jar getEnum trace if JGit is upgraded past 7.6.0.",
